CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "e6acf649-b95a-42ad-a464-eae802554253",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T03:29:03Z",
  "ticket_id": "7f42-e41f-a501-4007",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "(a) plugins/dso/hooks/pre-commit-intent-coverage-gate.sh invokes only the FAST checks (file existence + header parsing). NO test-runner invocation in pre-commit. Block-mode reserved for intent_with_no_test at closure-time only, detected via ticket-transition hook.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes the durable behavior of what the pre-commit hook invokes and when blocking occurs, not a one-time completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(b) 94ed-f55c's manifest-aware default validator (already registered with a03c-d55e's pluggable end-state-item-validator hook) ingests the findings JSON. ALL seven finding types (intent_with_no_test, test_artifact_missing_on_disk, test_artifact_fails, header_source_mismatch, dynamic_import_inconclusive, source_files_unresolved, file_impact_likely_stale) are explicitly enumerated as a contract requirement for 94ed's validator output mapping \u2014 the validator must register each type for rendering in the completion-verifier \"Intent Allocation Findings\" section.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability where the validator ingests and maps all seven finding types for ongoing rendering, not a one-time completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(c) .github/workflows/intent-coverage.yml invokes both scripts AND the (a)-step-iii test-pass validation step at CI time. Posts findings as PR comment via upsert-by-marker pattern: finds prior bot comment by the stable marker `COVERAGE_FINDINGS_<epic-id>` and edits it in place; if absent, posts new. One comment per PR, never a thread. Fallback when comment-write is unavailable (e.g., fork PRs with read-only GITHUB_TOKEN): write findings to the GHA job summary so the signal is not silently dropped.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable CI workflow behavior and communication patterns that persist after implementation, not a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(a) HAPPY PATH: Python + bash test fixtures with valid intent-claim headers and manifest entries pointing at them. Both scripts return zero findings.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability where test fixtures with valid headers exist and scripts return zero findings, phrased as an ongoing behavioral condition"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(b) INTENT_WITH_NO_TEST: fixture epic with 2 SCs, only one has a manifest entry. intent-coverage-check.sh surfaces intent_with_no_test for the uncovered SC. completion-verifier dispatch produces a non-empty \"Intent Allocation Findings\" section naming it.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability where tooling can detect and report intent coverage gaps"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(c) HEADER_SOURCE_MISMATCH: fixture Python test + fixture bash test both with valid intent-claim headers but no source-file symbol references. intent-header-source-check.sh surfaces header_source_mismatch for each.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable testing capability where mismatches between intent headers and source references are detected and surfaced by the check script"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(d) SOURCE_FILES_UNRESOLVED: intent_id whose manifest entry has no source_files field AND whose parent ticket file_impact is empty. intent-header-source-check.sh surfaces source_files_unresolved (warn, fail-open) and skips the (a+) check for that intent.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where the intent-header-source-check tool reliably identifies and handles unresolved source files by warning and skipping downstream checks"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(e) FILE_IMPACT_LIKELY_STALE: parent ticket file_impact references a path that doesn't exist on disk. intent-header-source-check.sh surfaces file_impact_likely_stale (warn) but still attempts source-symbol matching against the surviving file_impact entries.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior where the tool continues to attempt matching despite stale references, a property that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(f) DEFERRED_TEST OVERRIDE: manifest entry with deferred_test: true set. Closure attempt on the parent ticket does NOT block on intent_with_no_test for that intent.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where manifest entries with deferred_test flag have specific blocking semantics that persist after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(g) MISSING_SG: simulate sg absence on the runtime PATH. intent-header-source-check.sh emits dynamic_import_inconclusive (warn) for all test files; NO grep fallback is executed; pre-commit does NOT block.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where the security group simulation produces specific outcomes (warn level, no grep fallback, no pre-commit blocking) that persist after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(h) BACKWARD_COMPAT_94ED_LEGACY: manifest entry without source_files field AND without deferred_test field (pre-extension legacy schema). Scripts handle gracefully: source_files resolution falls back to parent ticket file_impact; absent deferred_test treated as false. Verifies the additive 94ed schema extension preserves backward compatibility for existing consumers.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system property\u2014the schema extension gracefully handles legacy manifest entries\u2014verified through backward-compatibility testing but phrased as ongoing behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "(i) MID_SPRINT_SC_ADDITION: fixture epic with 1 SC and 1 test_artifact registered passing; a 2nd SC is added to the epic description without registering a corresponding test_artifact. intent-coverage-check.sh surfaces intent_with_no_test for the new SC; completion-verifier dispatch produces non-empty \"Intent Allocation Findings\" section. Verifies the primary real-world miss pattern.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a specific test setup task and verification completion, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
